    "result_text": "All 28 tests pass with a clean build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation for pet owners, satisfying the Cp17 spec (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`, else `UNKNOWN`).\n\nFollowing the existing conventions of this Spring Boot / MapStruct / OpenAPI-generated codebase (the same pattern used for `displayName`, `initials`, `householdId`, `membershipTier`, etc.), the change has three parts:\n\n1. **`util/Localities.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper mirroring `Households`, holding the fixed city-to-region table and a `region(String city)` method that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` (null-safe, case-exact to match the pinned reference table in the tests).\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` DTO schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", \u2026)` expression deriving it from `owner.getCity()` via `Localities.region(...)`, so it's computed on every `toOwnerDto` (both create and GET responses).\n\nBecause it's a derived field computed at mapping time, no entity/schema/database changes were needed.\n\n**Verification:** `Cp17Tests` (known city \u2192 `NSW`, unknown city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 28, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
